WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.020
Good to have you on Planetarian Daily, Episode 102, coming to you on June 26th, 2026.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.180
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.140
C-animonies use a protein that reverses the usual role of a human immune component

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.260
to fight viruses. Researchers identified a protein in C-animonies

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.980
that resembles a human immune component yet performs the opposite function.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.400
This protein remains essential for blocking viral replication in the animals.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.840
The study used molecular and functional assays to confirm the reversed role.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.420
The finding shows that antiviral strategies diverged early in animal evolution

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.980
and that multiple effective pathways exist.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.800
Future work will test whether similar alternative mechanisms appear in other invertebrates.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.380
C-animonies maintain antiviral protection with a protein that inverts the role played by its

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:03.760
human counterpart. The reversal demonstrates that effective immune solutions are not limited to

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.420
the vertebrate playbook. Because the protein is required rather than inhibitory,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.440
it points to an independent evolutionary branch for innate antiviral defense.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:20.680
The next step is to determine whether similar inverted mechanisms exist in other early

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:26.020
branching animals and whether any components can be adapted for synthetic biology applications.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.740
Most people assume every animal fights viruses with roughly the same molecular toolkit that humans

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:39.220
use. That assumption does not hold. Right now your own cells rely on sensors that detect viral

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:47.500
RNA and trigger interferon responses. Yet C-animonies achieve protection by repurposing a structurally

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:54.580
similar protein to block replication through an opposite mechanism. A single memorable detail is

00:01:54.580 --> 00:02:00.160
that the anemone protein is essential for defense, even though it performs the reverse biochemical

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:07.020
task of its human homologue. This matters because drug developers sometimes assume conserved pathways

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:14.460
will respond similarly across species. The anemone case shows why that shortcut can miss entire

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:21.800
classes of solutions. One practical takeaway is to watch for future papers that map antiviral proteins

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:28.760
across additional invertebrate lineages. Those maps may reveal entirely new molecular strategies

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:35.740
rather than variations on the human theme. Now, shifting to microbial coordination that also

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:41.240
challenges standard assumptions about shared environments. Two common pathogens coordinate

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:47.580
copper availability in their shared environment to stabilize joint biofilms. The mechanism allows

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:54.240
the microbes to maintain structural integrity under metal stress. Experiments tracked copper fluxes

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:00.760
between the species and show that disrupting this exchange weakens the biofilm. The work maps copper

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:07.560
fluxes between species rather than within one. University of Oxford, geologists found chemical

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:13.040
and structural evidence of extensive earth-style magma chambers beneath the Martian surface.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:19.640
The systems formed without plate tectonics challenging prior models of planetary differentiation.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.720
Data came from meteorite analysis and orbital observations of crustal composition.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:32.160
The results refine understanding of how Mars cooled and lost its early magnetic field.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.240
This evidence emerged from combined analysis of meteorites and orbital crustal data.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:44.780
Attribution analysis shows the current European heat episode exceeds any plausible range without

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:51.620
anthropogenic climate change. Models that omit greenhouse gas forcing produce no comparable events.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:57.620
The study quantified the contribution of human emissions to both daytime and nighttime temperatures.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:02.840
Results strengthen the link between emissions and current extreme heat frequency.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.440
The analysis compared observed temperatures against scenarios lacking human influence.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:16.480
A new analysis finds that stomatal closure under elevated CO2 improves plant water use efficiency

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:23.480
less than earlier estimates predicted. Land surface models that assume large savings over estimate

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:30.720
future soil moisture in many regions. The study combines satellite observations with flux tower data

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.860
across multiple biomes. Revised projections indicate faster increases in drought risk.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.560
Satellite and flux tower records span several vegetation types.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:48.520
POSTEC and KENTEC teams developed an solution process that simultaneously adjusts electronic

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:55.340
and magnetic properties in oxide thin films. The method produces embedded nanoparticles whose size

00:04:55.340 --> 00:05:01.360
and distribution control conductivity and spin behavior. Published in advanced materials,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.520
the work demonstrates reversible switching under modest temperature changes.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.240
The approach offers a route to new spin-tronic and memory devices,

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.340
size and distribution of the nanoparticles directly tune the film properties.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:24.060
HEFAY institutes researchers measured the upper critical field of LA4NI3010.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.640
Under pressure and found nearly isotropic behavior, the result differs from the strong

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:36.180
ionisotropy seen in many coupe rates. High pressure transport and magnetization data support

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:41.420
the finding. It narrows possible pairing mechanisms for nickel-based superconductors.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.580
The measurements were performed under applied pressure conditions.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:52.780
An international journal of technology enhanced learning study tracked students before and after

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:58.900
targeted computational thinking instruction. Both self-reported skill ratings and objective

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:04.340
performance on novel problems rose. The gains appeared across different disciplines.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:10.860
The work supports wider integration of computational thinking modules in undergraduate curricula.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:16.000
Performance improvements were documented on problems not previously encountered.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:22.740
Gaia data revealed a stellar passage that perturbed the Oort cloud and increased common influx.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:28.360
Orbital simulations show the perturbation continues to shape comet trajectories today.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:34.920
The work was presented at the American Astronomical Society Division on Dynamical Astronomy Meeting.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.880
It links a single historical event to ongoing solar system dynamics.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.880
The simulations incorporated updated Gaia astrometric measurements.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:51.180
From microbial interactions that affect health, shift to land management practices that

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.800
directly influence soil and water systems supporting human food production.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.380
Wageningen University researchers found that economic and environmental benefits of regenerative

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:09.260
practices vary sharply with water availability and manure supply. Farms in some European regions

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:16.180
showed clear gains. Others did not. The regionomics project used paired field comparisons and

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:22.120
economic modeling. Water availability and manure supply determined whether practices deliver

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:28.180
measurable improvements. Recommendations now emphasize site-specific planning rather than

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:35.160
uniform adoption. From variable land-based interventions turned to a clear success story of nutrient

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:41.500
management that improved freshwater systems at scale. Nutrient reductions from improved wastewater

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:47.640
treatment halted or reversed deoxygenation trends across monitored Chinese lakes and rivers.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:55.280
The effect persisted even as regional temperatures rose. The Nature Geoscience study combined long-term

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:59.840
monitoring data with modeling to separate management impacts from climate effects.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:06.100
Continued nutrient controls appear sufficient to maintain gains. Penn's sociologist

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:11.180
Pilar Gunalon's Pons and colleagues compared household data across parent types.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:17.660
Same-sex couples maintained more balance paid and unpaid worksplates than different sex couples

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:22.580
after parenthood. The pattern held after controlling for income and education.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:27.500
The findings highlight how gender norms shape post-child labor allocation.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:34.100
Data-spaned multiple household surveys. A University of North Carolina trial tested

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:41.280
messages encouraging offline meetups among lonely 18 to 29-year-olds. Participants who received

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:47.120
the prompts reported higher rates of in-person interaction. The Journal of Adolescent Health

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:53.240
study measured both self-report and behavioral outcomes. The approach offers a low-cost

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:59.480
complement to existing loneliness interventions. The trial focused on young adults reporting loneliness.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:06.020
From large-scale environmental recovery moved to a material's advance that could improve internal

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:12.860
medical imaging. Researchers fabricated soft hydrogel fibers, hundreds of micrometers wide

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:20.120
that carry light with low loss. The fibers are flexible enough to navigate narrow ducts. Early

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:27.140
tests target early breast cancer detection inside small ducts. Further material optimization is

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:34.060
underway to reach clinical resolution. From engineered biomaterials for imaging close with a natural

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:41.800
biomaterial whose assembly rules have just been decoded. University of Salzburg scientists decoded

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:48.560
the composition of Tintin and Karana after more than two centuries of study. The shells consist of

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:55.240
proteins that spontaneously assemble into a UV absorbing resilient material. This is the first

00:09:55.240 --> 00:10:03.300
identified biomaterial produced by a eukaryotic protest. The discovery establishes Tintinids as a new

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:10.600
system for biomaterial research. Next time keep an eye on new orbital data that may clarify how ancient

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:16.820
stellar passages continue to shape comet trajectories. That covers today's science and health news.

